{
  "hypothesis": "The current policy over-weights raw failure_rate and invalid_count, causing repeated attempts on recovery (high failure_rate, invalid_count=2) despite zero gain, while under-exploring tools (low attempted, moderate failure_rate) and memory (high last_gain but attempted=2). A policy that penalizes stagnation and invalid_count more strongly, and rewards last_gain and success_rate, will shift exploration toward modules with demonstrated or potential gains (memory, tools) and away from repeatedly failing recovery.",
  "policy": {
    "score": {
      "op": "add",
      "args": [
        {
          "op": "mul",
          "args": [
            2,
            {
              "op": "sub",
              "args": [
                1,
                {"var": "attempted"}
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "op": "add",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "mul",
              "args": [
                0.5,
                {"var": "failure_rate"}
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "add",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "mul",
                  "args": [
                    1.5,
                    {"var": "stagnation"}
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "add",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "mul",
                      "args": [
                        2,
                        {"var": "invalid_count"}
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "add",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "mul",
                          "args": [
                            3,
                            {"var": "last_gain"}
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "mul",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            {"var": "success_rate"}
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "branches": 2
  },
  "predicted_decision_change": "Recovery's score will drop sharply due to invalid_count=2 and stagnation=0 (but high failure_rate and zero last_gain), while memory's score rises from last_gain=0.286 and success_rate=1.0, and tools' score rises from low attempted=0 and moderate failure_rate=0.333. The next two branches will likely target memory and tools instead of recovery, reducing repeated invalid attempts on recovery and exploring remaining real defects in tools."
}

